  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let PPP be a polynomial in nnn variables given by:\n\nP(x1,x2,…,xn)=(k+x1+x2+⋯+xn)mP(x_1, x_2, \\ldots,x_{n}) = (k + x_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_{n})^{m}P(x1​,x2​,…,xn​)=(k+x1​+x2​+⋯+xn​)mHere nnn, kkk and mmm are positive integers. Find the sum of all coefficients of the terms of the polynomial which have even powers in each of the nnn variables and output it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\nNote that the constant term's coefficient is also included in the sum. Please see the sample IO and Explanation for details.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nFirst line will contain the number of testcases TTT\nEach testcase will consist of single line with 333 positive integers nnn, kkk and mmm in that order\n###Output:\r\nOutput a single line containing the required sum modulo 100000000710000000071000000007 for each testcase.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103\n1≤n≤1051 \\leq n \\leq 10^51≤n≤105\n1≤k≤1061 \\leq k \\leq 10^61≤k≤106\n1≤m≤1061 \\leq m \\leq 10^61≤m≤106\nSum of nnn over all testcases ≤105\\leq 10^5≤105\n###Subtasks\n\n\n30 points : n=1n = 1n=1\n70 points : original constraints\n###Sample Input:\n\n`3\r\n2 1 2\r\n3 3 2\r\n2 5 4\n`###Sample Output:\n\n`3\r\n12\r\n933\n`###Explanation:\n\n\nFor the first testcase, the given polynomial is (1+x1+x2)2(1 + x_1 + x_2)^2(1+x1​+x2​)2 which can be expanded as: 1+x12+x22+2x1+2x2+2x1x21 + x_1^2 + x_2^2 + 2x_1 + 2x_2 + 2x_1x_21+x12​+x22​+2x1​+2x2​+2x1​x2​\r\nThe terms with even power in all variables are 111, x12x_1^2x12​ and x22x_2^2x22​. The sum of their coefficients is 1+1+1=31 + 1 + 1 = 31+1+1=3.\nFor the second testcase, the given polynomial is (3+x1+x2+x3)2(3+x_1+x_2+x_3)^2(3+x1​+x2​+x3​)2 which can be expanded as: 2x1x2+2x1x3+6x1+x12+6x2+x22+6x3+2x2x3+x32+92x_1x_2+2x_1x_3+6x_1+x_1^2+6x_2+x_2^2+6x_3+2x_2x_3+x_3^2+92x1​x2​+2x1​x3​+6x1​+x12​+6x2​+x22​+6x3​+2x2​x3​+x32​+9\r\nThe terms with even power in all variables are x12x_1^2x12​, x22x_2^2x22​, x32x_3^2x32​ and 999. The sum of their coefficients is 1+1+1+9=121 + 1 + 1  + 9 = 121+1+1+9=12.\nFor the third testcase, the given polynomial is (5+x1+x2)4(5 + x_1 + x_2)^4(5+x1​+x2​)4 which can be expanded as: 625+500x1+150x12+20x13+x14+500x2+300x1x2+60x12x2+4x13x2+150x22+60x1x22+6x12x22+20x23+4x1x23+x24625+500x_1+150x_1^2+20x_1^3+x_1^4+500x_2+300x_1x_2+60x_1^2x_2+4x_1^3\n x_2+150x_2^2+60x_1x_2^2+6x_1^2x_2^2+20x_2^3+4x_1x_2^3+x_2^4625+500x1​+150x12​+20x13​+x14​+500x2​+300x1​x2​+60x12​x2​+4x13​x2​+150x22​+60x1​x22​+6x12​x22​+20x23​+4x1​x23​+x24​\r\nThe terms with even power in all variables are 625625625, 150x12150x_1^2150x12​, x14x_1^4x14​, 150x22150x_2^2150x22​, 6x12x226x_1^2x_2^26x12​x22​ and x24x_2^4x24​. The sum of their coefficients is 625+150+1+150+6+1=933625 + 150 + 1 + 150 + 6 + 1 = 933625+150+1+150+6+1=933",
